<p>The work involves improvements to<strong> Route 5 in the province of Chiloé along an extension of 126 km</strong> and a route that crosses the districts of Ancud, Dalcahue, Castro and Chonchi. The project starts at the southern access to the future bridge <strong>over the Chacao Channel and ends at the fork in the northern access to Chonchi</strong>. It also considers operation and maintenance of approximately 16 kilometers of road with a bi-directional roadway profile, corresponding to the Castro Bypass.</p>
